          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Informally, a
            %strong free functor
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            – part of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-forgetful+adjunction"} free-forgetful adjunction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            is informal;
            %em any
            functor might be viewed as forgetful, so
            %em any
            left adjoint might be viewed as free, while in practice only some are.)
          %p
            Formally, with respect to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg(C)
            the corresponding category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+a+monad"} algebras over a monad
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+an+algebraic+theory"} algebras over an algebraic theory
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+an+operad"} algebras over an operad
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %strong
              free
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg(C) \to C
          %p
            Such a functor may be thought of as sending any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %em freely generated
            by it.
          %h3#free_objects Free objects
          %p
            In general, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: C \to D
            is thought of as a forgetful functor and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: D \to C
            is its left adjoint, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(x)
            is the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free C-object
            on an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p
            More generally, even if the entire left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            doesn’t exist, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free object
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            can be defined using a universal property, as “what the value of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(x)
            would be if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            existed.” Conversely, if a free object on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            exists for
            %em all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            can be assembled from them.
          %h3#cofree_functors Cofree functors
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"}> Dually
            , a
            %strong cofree functor
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            to a forgetful functor.
          %p For the classical functors which forget algebraic structure, cofree functors are less common than free functors.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Classically, examples of free constructions were characterized by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            the universal property states that any map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to G
            as sets uniquely extends to a group homomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X) \to G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-forgetful+adjunction"} free-forgetful adjunction
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \downarrow U)
            (where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is the forgetful functor out of the category of algebras, see e.g. the proof of Freyd’s general
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
          %h3#for_free_functors For free functors
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+monoid"} free monoid
                functor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mon"} Mon
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
                functor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
                for a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+group"} free group
                functor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
                functor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mon"} Mon
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              %p in the abelian case in particular:
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group+of+a+commutative+monoid"} Grothendieck group completion
                functor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CMon"} CMon
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
                functor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelianization"} abelianization
                functor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
                functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Grph
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo ,
                          %mi r
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grph_{d,r} \to
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+operad"} free operad
                functor;
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitisation"} unitisation
                functor
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rng"} Rng
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ring"} Ring
          %p
            Free constructions
            %em on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"}> free cocompletion
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+coproduct+completion"} free coproduct completion
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+completion"} idempotent completion
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+completion"} Cauchy completion
          %p
            One formal sort of free functor is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C^T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^T
            is its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            (the category of
            = succeed "-algebras)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            A general way to construct free functors is with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+construction+of+free+algebras"} transfinite construction of free algebras
            (in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set-theoretic
            foundations), or with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+type"} inductive type
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"} higher inductive type
            (in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type-theoretic
            foundations).
          %h3#for_cofree_functors For cofree functors
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofree+coalgebra"} cofree coalgebra
                on a vector space. More generally, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
                in a symmetric monoidal category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Prop
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prop(M)
                its associated
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PROP"} PROP
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a monoidal
                = succeed "-category," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                = succeed "-coalgebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                may be identified with a monoidal
                = succeed "-functor" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Prop
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi M
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prop(M)^{op} \to C
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Coalg
                        %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Coalg_C \to C
                has a right adjoint, and this forgetful functor is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonadic+functor"} comonadic
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                is a monoid, the forgetful functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mi M
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^M \to Set
                on (left)
                = succeed "-sets" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi M
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto \hom(M, X)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                acts on functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi M
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: M \to X
                according to the rule
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi m
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi m
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi m
                        %mo ′
                        %mi m
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (m f)(m') = f(m' m)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^C \to Set/C_0
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
                the set of objects of a category
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                is complete and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: C \to D
                is a functor between small categories, the functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mi D
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^f: V^D \to V^C
                has a right adjoint (although
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^f
                will not normally be comonadic in this generality).
            %li
              %p
                The forgetful functor
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cat
                        %mo →
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat \to Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                for which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K X
                is a category whose objects are elements of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and where there is exactly one morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \to y
                for any
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in X
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K X
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                When
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
